            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "おねがいします (onegai shimasu)。 — o-ne-ga-i shi-ma-su — please; I request it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The pieces make the social direction visible: respectful o-, negai “request or wish,” and polite shimasu “do.” Learn the whole as the courteous request ending. Do not translate each piece while speaking."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The common kanji spelling can wait. This chapter earns the sound and social use first, without switching writing systems mid-ramp."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "onegaishimasu becomes choose a polite request",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *onegaishimasu* → choose **a polite request**]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "onegaishimasu once at an even pace",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *onegaishimasu* once at an even pace]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "JOIN",
              "instruction": "mō ichido, onegaishimasu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU JOIN: *mō ichido, onegaishimasu*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Keep the tone even and courteous; volume does not make the request more polite."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: Japan Foundation Irodori Starter lesson 2, pp. 1–3."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "JA-C09-onegaishimasu-job",
              "prompt": "What polite expression closes the request one more time, please?",
              "assesses": [
                "JA-LEX-ONEGAI-SHIMASU"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "おねがいします",
                "onegaishimasu",
                "おねがいします。"
